{
  "description": "Every container image the integration tests (crates/*/tests) and spicescript start, by the registry/repository:tag they name it by, and the digest that tag named when it was recorded: the image index's for a multi-platform image, so each host still pulls its own platform. The harnesses start a container only from an image listed here, pulled and run as registry/repository:tag@digest (crates/container-images), so a tag that moves, or a registry that serves other content under it, cannot change what a test runs in a job that holds credentials; an image not listed is refused. Keys are canonical (docker.io/library/postgres:18 for postgres:18) and name a release, never a tag such as latest that moves to each one. To add or move a pin, run .github/scripts/pin_container_images.py --write <image>, which reads the digest from the registry anonymously, and review the change; --refresh reports pins whose tag has since moved. The container-images crate's unit tests fail when a test source names an image this file does not pin, or this file pins one nothing names.",
